// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: new rule
// Title: Proxy Execution Via Mscopilot.EXE GPU-Launcher
// Sigma ID: 6acb22bc-6287-4afd-9b57-9c4d6bc2e215
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects abuse of the signed Microsoft Copilot Electron binary via the "--gpu-launcher" argument
//   to proxy-execute an arbitrary command. The legitimate value points to the GPU process; attackers
//   set it to a shell command for signed-binary proxy execution.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Mscopilot/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c5875f6ddd2f5087d0f0a63a34a2ed4468a9d328/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_mscopilot_gpu_launcher_proxy_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\mscopilot.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mscopilot_proxy.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "--gpu-launcher=" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "cmd" or ProcessCommandLine contains "powershell" or ProcessCommandLine contains "pwsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "&&" or ProcessCommandLine contains "rundll32" or ProcessCommandLine contains "regsvr32" or ProcessCommandLine contains "mshta")
